---
import '@fontsource/bricolage-grotesque/500.css';
import '@fontsource/bricolage-grotesque/700.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/webp" href={base + "/logo-mark.webp"} />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://twistor.co/logo-mark.webp" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Twistor | The company that does it all" />
    <meta
      property="og:description"
      content="Twistor builds AI systems that answer your phones, recover your revenue, and run your operations. One platform, every product."
    />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://twistor.co/" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="Twistor | The company that does it all" />
    <meta
      name="twitter:description"
      content="Twistor builds AI systems that answer your phones, recover your revenue, and run your operations. One platform, every product."
    />
    <title>Twistor | The company that does it all</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Twistor builds AI systems that answer your phones, recover your revenue, and run your operations. One platform, every product."
    />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href={base + "/cinematic/engine/cinematic.css"} />
    <link rel="preload" as="image" href="cinematic/media/poster.webp" fetchpriority="high" />
    <style>
:root{--brand-serif:Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;--ink:#1C1A17;--paper:#FAF7F2;--accent:#FF5A1F;}
body{margin:0;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper);line-height:1.6;}
.wordmark{font-weight:700;font-size:1.25rem;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;}
.wordmark span{color:var(--accent);}
header[data-overlay]{display:flex;gap:24px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:16px 24px;}
header[data-overlay] nav a{margin-right:16px;color:inherit;text-decoration:none;font-weight:500;}
.cta{background:var(--accent);color:var(--ink);padding:10px 18px;border-radius:8px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;}
#flight-track{height:calc(5472px + 100vh);}
.flight-sticky{--field:#FAF7F2;--field-contrast:#1C1A17;background:var(--field);}
.flight-sticky[data-state="establish"]{--field:#FAF7F2;--field-contrast:#1C1A17;}
.flight-sticky[data-state="enter"]{--field:#1C1A17;--field-contrast:#FAF7F2;}
.flight-sticky[data-state="trades"]{--field:#1C1A17;--field-contrast:#FF5A1F;}
.flight-sticky[data-state="road"]{--field:#FAF7F2;--field-contrast:#1C1A17;}
.flight-sticky[data-state="dispatch"]{--field:#FAF7F2;--field-contrast:#B5430E;}
.flight-sticky[data-state="data"]{--field:#1C1A17;--field-contrast:#FF5A1F;}
.poster-first{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;z-index:1;}
header[data-overlay="PersistentNav"]{position:fixed;top:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:6;background:var(--paper);border-bottom:2px solid var(--ink);}
[data-overlay="ScrollHint"]{left:24px;bottom:24px;z-index:3;margin:0;font-weight:600;color:var(--field-contrast);}
[data-overlay="KineticHeadline"]{left:24px;top:15%;z-index:3;max-width:11em;color:var(--field-contrast);font-size:clamp(2.1rem,5vw,4.2rem);line-height:1.05;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-0.02em;}
[data-overlay="ProgressCard"]{left:24px;bottom:24px;z-index:3;max-width:400px;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);border:2px solid var(--ink);border-radius:16px;padding:18px 22px;}
[data-overlay="ProgressCard"] ol{margin:0;padding-left:20px;}
[data-overlay="ProgressCard"] li{margin-bottom:8px;}
[data-overlay="HotspotLayer"]{right:24px;top:96px;z-index:3;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;}
[data-overlay="RoomLabel"]{left:24px;top:84px;z-index:3;margin:0;background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);padding:6px 14px;border-radius:999px;font-weight:600;}
[data-overlay="PillNav"]{right:24px;bottom:24px;z-index:3;display:flex;gap:8px;}
[data-overlay="PillNav"] button{background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);border:2px solid var(--ink);border-radius:999px;padding:10px 18px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;}
[data-overlay="TickerBand"]{left:0;right:0;bottom:0;z-index:3;background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);padding:10px 0;--ticker-duration:28s;}
[data-overlay="BackControl"]{left:24px;bottom:24px;z-index:3;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);border:2px solid var(--ink);border-radius:999px;padding:10px 18px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;}
@media (max-width:640px){
[data-overlay="ProgressCard"]{left:16px;right:16px;bottom:88px;max-width:none;}
[data-overlay="PillNav"]{right:16px;bottom:16px;}
[data-overlay="RoomLabel"]{left:16px;top:76px;}
[data-overlay="ScrollHint"]{left:16px;bottom:16px;}
[data-overlay="KineticHeadline"]{left:16px;top:12%;}
[data-overlay="HotspotLayer"]{right:16px;top:88px;}
[data-overlay="BackControl"]{left:16px;bottom:16px;}
}
#ambient{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:none;}
html[data-tier="C"] #ambient{display:block;}
.poster-set{display:none;}
html[data-tier="D"] .poster-set,html[data-reduced="true"] .poster-set{display:block;}
html[data-tier="D"] #flight-canvas,html[data-reduced="true"] #flight-canvas{display:none;}
.poster-set figure{margin:0 0 24px;}
.poster-set img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block;}
.hotspot{border-radius:50%;border:2px solid var(--field-contrast);background:transparent;color:var(--field-contrast);font-size:1.25rem;cursor:pointer;}
.money-story li{margin-bottom:8px;}
#structured-view,section.work{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;padding:48px 24px;}
#structured-view article{margin-bottom:20px;}
.work img{max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:12px;}
.credits{color:#5F5A54;font-size:0.9rem;}
footer{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;}
/* Site type wiring (TW-1050 port): Bricolage Grotesque is the site's
   display face; the rebuild's body type stays system-ui as built. */
h1, h2, h3, .kh-line { font-family: 'Bricolage Grotesque', system-ui, sans-serif; }

    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
<header data-overlay="PersistentNav" data-state="ALL" data-interactive="true"><p class="wordmark">Twistor<span>.</span></p><nav><a href="#fact-trades-front-office">Trades AI Front Office</a><a href="#fact-dispatch-os">Dispatch OS</a><a href="#fact-data-analytics">Managed Data + Analytics</a></nav><a class="cta" href="#fact-cta-book-a-demo">Book a demo</a></header>
<main>
  <div class="flight-track" id="flight-track">
    <div class="flight-sticky">
      <video id="ambient" src="cinematic/media/c/scene.mp4" muted loop playsinline aria-hidden="true"></video>
      <img class="poster-first" src="cinematic/media/poster.webp" alt="" aria-hidden="true" fetchpriority="high">
      <canvas id="flight-canvas" width="1600" height="900"
              aria-label="Cinematic flight. All information in this flight is listed in text below."></canvas>
<p data-overlay="ScrollHint" data-state="establish">Scroll to explore</p>
<section data-overlay="KineticHeadline" data-state="enter"><p class="kh-line"><span class="kh-line-inner" data-line data-state="enter" data-reveal-frame="6">The phone rings.</span></p><p class="kh-line"><span class="kh-line-inner" data-line data-state="enter" data-reveal-frame="18">The shop is under a truck.</span></p><p class="kh-line"><span class="kh-line-inner" data-line data-state="enter" data-reveal-frame="30">The caller books somebody else.</span></p><p class="kh-line kh-accent"><span class="kh-line-inner" data-line data-state="enter" data-reveal-frame="42">Unless Twistor answers first.</span></p></section>
<section data-overlay="ProgressCard" data-state="trades" aria-live="off"><ol class="money-story"><li><strong>The missed call</strong> Every missed call is a job somebody else books. For a working shop, the leak runs to thousands a month.</li><li><strong>Booked, not lost</strong> Twistor answers on the first ring, triages the urgency, and books the job straight onto your dispatch board.</li><li><strong>Invoice paid</strong> The job is dispatched, done, and invoiced. Nothing rots in a follow-up pile.</li></ol></section>
<div data-overlay="HotspotLayer" data-state="trades" data-interactive="true"><button type="button" class="hotspot" data-fact="missed-call-cost" style="width:48px;height:48px" aria-label="The missed call">+</button><button type="button" class="hotspot" data-fact="booking-flow" style="width:48px;height:48px" aria-label="Booked, not lost">+</button><button type="button" class="hotspot" data-fact="invoice-paid" style="width:48px;height:48px" aria-label="Invoice paid">+</button></div>
<p data-overlay="RoomLabel" data-state="trades">FIG. 01 / Dispatch board</p>
<nav data-overlay="PillNav" data-state="trades" data-interactive="true" aria-label="Jump to a state"><button type="button" data-target="trades">Trades</button><button type="button" data-target="dispatch">Dispatch</button><button type="button" data-target="data">Data</button></nav>
<div data-overlay="TickerBand" data-state="road" aria-hidden="true"><div class="ticker-track"><span class="ticker-item">Trades AI Front Office</span><span class="ticker-item">Dispatch OS</span><span class="ticker-item">Managed Data + Analytics</span><span class="ticker-item">Compliance Evidence Agent</span><span class="ticker-item">Trades AI Front Office</span><span class="ticker-item">Dispatch OS</span><span class="ticker-item">Managed Data + Analytics</span><span class="ticker-item">Compliance Evidence Agent</span></div></div>
<p data-overlay="RoomLabel" data-state="dispatch">FIG. 02 / The answered call</p>
<nav data-overlay="PillNav" data-state="dispatch" data-interactive="true" aria-label="Jump to a state"><button type="button" data-target="trades">Trades</button><button type="button" data-target="dispatch">Dispatch</button><button type="button" data-target="data">Data</button></nav>
<p data-overlay="RoomLabel" data-state="data">FIG. 03 / Data, wired clean</p>
<nav data-overlay="PillNav" data-state="data" data-interactive="true" aria-label="Jump to a state"><button type="button" data-target="trades">Trades</button><button type="button" data-target="dispatch">Dispatch</button><button type="button" data-target="data">Data</button></nav>
<button type="button" data-overlay="BackControl" data-state="data" data-interactive="true" data-target="trades">Back</button>
    </div>
  </div>
<section class="poster-set" aria-label="Segment posters"><figure><img src="cinematic/media/d/establish.webp" alt="Rooftop wide at working height: two techs at an open package unit under a big sky, Twistor wordmark nav on top, the twisted-T floating center. Poster frame = this segment&#x27;s first frame."><figcaption>establish: guide, Twistor twisted-T mark, FLOAT. Rooftop wide at working height: two techs at an open package unit under a big sky, Twistor wordmark nav on top, the twisted-T floating center. Poster frame = this segment&#x27;s first frame.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="cinematic/media/d/enter.webp" alt="The drill goes in: the path stroke draws across the unit and the guide rides its tip while the kinetic headline builds the missed-call story. Travel segments sample at 12 fps per REA 3.1."><figcaption>enter: guide, Twistor twisted-T mark, PATH_TIP. The drill goes in: the path stroke draws across the unit and the guide rides its tip while the kinetic headline builds the missed-call story. Travel segments sample at 12 fps per REA 3.1.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="cinematic/media/d/trades.webp" alt="01 Trades AI Front Office. The gauges read right because the call was answered: ProgressCard counts the money story (missed call, booked job, paid invoice), hotspots on the three proof points."><figcaption>trades: guide, Twistor twisted-T mark, PARK at prop-dispatch-board. 01 Trades AI Front Office. The gauges read right because the call was answered: ProgressCard counts the money story (missed call, booked job, paid invoice), hotspots on the three proof points.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="cinematic/media/d/road.webp" alt="The road between services: hands tape the line set while the stroke carries the guide onward and the ticker names the product line. The divider panel of the reference folds into this travel, per the teardown."><figcaption>road: guide, Twistor twisted-T mark, PATH_TIP. The road between services: hands tape the line set while the stroke carries the guide onward and the ticker names the product line. The divider panel of the reference folds into this travel, per the teardown.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="cinematic/media/d/dispatch.webp" alt="02 Dispatch OS. The human on the headset is the product working: one board runs the phones and the schedule."><figcaption>dispatch: guide, Twistor twisted-T mark, PARK at prop-headset. 02 Dispatch OS. The human on the headset is the product working: one board runs the phones and the schedule.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="cinematic/media/d/data.webp" alt="03 Managed Data + Analytics. The guide drifts past the panel the way the SLICK capsule drifts its dwell: the systems underneath, wired clean, reported in plain English."><figcaption>data: guide, Twistor twisted-T mark, DRIFT at prop-data-pipeline. 03 Managed Data + Analytics. The guide drifts past the panel the way the SLICK capsule drifts its dwell: the systems underneath, wired clean, reported in plain English.</figcaption></figure></section>
  <section id="structured-view" aria-label="Full information in text form">
    <h2>Everything on this page, in plain text</h2>
<article data-fact="brand" id="fact-brand"><h3>Twistor</h3><p>The company that does it all. Twistor builds AI systems that answer your phones, recover your revenue, and run your operations. One platform, every product.</p></article>
<article data-fact="cta-book-a-demo" id="fact-cta-book-a-demo"><h3>Book a demo</h3><p>Book a demo: thirty minutes, your numbers, no pitch deck theater.</p></article>
<article data-fact="missed-call-cost" id="fact-missed-call-cost"><h3>The missed call</h3><p>Every missed call is a job somebody else books. For a working shop, the leak runs to thousands a month.</p></article>
<article data-fact="booking-flow" id="fact-booking-flow"><h3>Booked, not lost</h3><p>Twistor answers on the first ring, triages the urgency, and books the job straight onto your dispatch board.</p></article>
<article data-fact="invoice-paid" id="fact-invoice-paid"><h3>Invoice paid</h3><p>The job is dispatched, done, and invoiced. Nothing rots in a follow-up pile.</p></article>
<article data-fact="trades-front-office" id="fact-trades-front-office"><h3>Trades AI Front Office</h3><p>For HVAC, plumbing, roofing, and electrical shops: AI reception that answers every call, triages urgency, and posts jobs straight to your dispatch board. Built for the trades first, because missed calls are missed revenue. Every call answered. Every urgent job triaged.</p></article>
<article data-fact="dispatch-os" id="fact-dispatch-os"><h3>Dispatch OS</h3><p>Jobs arrive by phone, email, or web. AI answers, triages, schedules, and confirms, while you watch a single dispatch board. One board that runs your phones and your schedule.</p></article>
<article data-fact="dental-front-office" id="fact-dental-front-office"><h3>Dental AI Front Office</h3><p>AI answers every call, confirms appointments, texts back missed calls in under a minute, and books directly inside your practice management software, with a monthly report showing recovered revenue. Never lose a patient to voicemail again.</p></article>
<article data-fact="compliance-agent" id="fact-compliance-agent"><h3>Compliance Evidence Agent</h3><p>An agent living in your repos and cloud accounts, continuously collecting SOC 2 and HIPAA evidence and opening PRs when something drifts.</p></article>
<article data-fact="data-analytics" id="fact-data-analytics"><h3>Managed Data + Analytics</h3><p>Pipelines from your SaaS tools into a clean warehouse, dashboards you actually read, and a monthly KPI memo in plain English. Your data team, done for you.</p></article>
<article data-fact="twistor-core" id="fact-twistor-core"><h3>Twistor Core</h3><p>Every product above runs on one platform underneath it all: Twistor Core. One data layer, one agent standard, one bill.</p></article>
<article data-fact="trades" id="fact-trades"><h3>Trades</h3><p>Segment: Trades AI Front Office.</p></article>
<article data-fact="dispatch" id="fact-dispatch"><h3>Dispatch</h3><p>Segment: Dispatch OS.</p></article>
<article data-fact="data" id="fact-data"><h3>Data</h3><p>Segment: Managed Data + Analytics.</p></article>
<article data-fact="prop-dispatch-board" id="fact-prop-dispatch-board"><h3>Dispatch board</h3><p>FIG. 01 / Dispatch board. The first stop on the flight: every answered call lands here as a booked job.</p></article>
<article data-fact="prop-headset" id="fact-prop-headset"><h3>The answered call</h3><p>FIG. 02 / The answered call. The second stop on the flight: a person and an agent on the same board, on the same call.</p></article>
<article data-fact="prop-data-pipeline" id="fact-prop-data-pipeline"><h3>Data, wired clean</h3><p>FIG. 03 / Data, wired clean. The third stop on the flight: the systems underneath the shop, wired into one clean pipeline.</p></article>
<article data-fact="The phone rings." class="fact-line"><p>The phone rings.</p></article>
<article data-fact="The shop is under a truck." class="fact-line"><p>The shop is under a truck.</p></article>
<article data-fact="The caller books somebody else." class="fact-line"><p>The caller books somebody else.</p></article>
<article data-fact="Unless Twistor answers first." class="fact-line"><p>Unless Twistor answers first.</p></article>
  </section>
  <section class="work" aria-label="Selected work">
    <h2>Selected work</h2>
    <figure>
      <img src="cinematic/media/work/8486972.jpg" alt="Plumber in a yellow hard hat and hi-vis vest, pipe wrench in hand, looking up at the work.">
      <figcaption>The work itself. Photo by Kindel Media on Pexels.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure>
      <img src="cinematic/media/work/5463580.jpg" alt="Close-up of hands running a leak detector along a condenser coil.">
      <figcaption>Evidence, collected by hand before it is collected by software. Photo by José Andrés Pacheco Cortes on Pexels.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
</main>
<footer>
  <button id="view-toggle" type="button">View: Full / Light</button>
  <p class="credits">Photography: José Andrés Pacheco Cortes, Kindel Media, and Pexels contributors, under the Pexels License (credits in PHOTO-MANIFEST.md). Prepared by Twistor Holdings LLC.</p>
</footer>
    <script src="../scripts/cinematic-home.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
